[agent:result]     Parameters:
[agent:result]         name: Name of the feature view to create.
[agent:result]         query: Feature store `Query`.
[agent:result]         version: Version of the feature view to create.
[agent:result]         description: A string describing the contents of the feature view to improve discoverability for Data Scientists.
[agent:result]         labels:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names constituting the prediction label/feature of the feature view.
[agent:result]             When replaying a `Query` during model inference, the label features can be omitted from the feature vector retrieval.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `[]`, no label.
[agent:result]         inference_helper_columns:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names that are not used in training the model itself but can be used during batch or online inference for extra information.
[agent:result]             Inference helper column name(s) must be part of the `Query` object.
[agent:result]             If inference helper column name(s) belong to feature group that is part of a `Join` with `prefix` defined, then this prefix needs to be prepended to the original column name when defining `inference_helper_columns` list.
[agent:result]             When replaying a `Query` during model inference, the inference helper columns optionally can be omitted during batch (`get_batch_data`) and will be omitted during online  inference (`get_feature_vector(s)`).
[agent:result]             To get inference helper column(s) during online inference use `get_inference_helper(s)` method.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `[], no helper columns.
[agent:result]         training_helper_columns:
[agent:result]             A list of feature names that are not the part of the model schema itself but can be used during training as a helper for extra information.
[agent:result]             Training helper column name(s) must be part of the `Query` object.
[agent:result]             If training helper column name(s) belong to feature group that is part of a `Join` with `prefix` defined, then this prefix needs to prepended to the original column name when defining `training_helper_columns` list.
[agent:result]             When replaying a `Query` during model inference, the training helper columns will be omitted during both batch and online inference.
[agent:result]             Training helper columns can be optionally fetched with training data.
[agent:result]             For more details see documentation for feature view's get training data methods.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `[]`, no training helper columns.
[agent:result]         transformation_functions:
[agent:result]             Model Dependent Transformation functions attached to the feature view.
[agent:result]             It can be a list of list of user defined functions defined using the hopsworks `@udf` decorator.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `None`, no transformations.
[agent:result]         logging_enabled: If true, enable feature logging for the feature view.
[agent:result]         extra_log_columns:
[agent:result]             Extra columns to be logged in addition to the features used in the feature view.
[agent:result]             It can be a list of Feature objects or list a dictionaries that contains the the name and type of the columns as keys.
[agent:result]             Defaults to `None`, no extra log columns.
